        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: हमला",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हमला — hamlā — \"an attack\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दुश्मन ने रात को क़िले पर हमला किया। duśman ne rāt ko qile par hamlā kiyā. The enemy attacked the fort at night."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हमला (hamlā) is usually traced, through Persian, to Arabic ḥamla, \"a charge, an onset\". What is attacked takes पर: क़िले पर हमला."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
